# The file everybody forgets, and the one that makes `COPY . .` safe.
#
# Without it, the build context is the whole repository: the git history, the
# virtual environment, the test data, the coverage reports and, on somebody's
# machine, a .env file with real credentials in it. All of it is uploaded to the
# daemon, and whatever the Dockerfile copies ends up in a layer that anybody who
# can pull the image can unpack.

.git
.github
.gitignore

# Anything that could hold a secret. This block is the reason the file exists.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
**/credentials

# Local environments and caches: large, machine specific, and never wanted.
.venv
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage

# Tests and tooling live in the builder stage, which installs them itself.
tests/
ship/
infra/
k8s/
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# Data. The repository's datasets are synthetic and they are still 40 MB of
# build context that the service never reads.
data/
*.csv
*.sqlite
